<Base title="About Us" description="Who we are and why The Body Explained exists.">
  <div class="page">
<h1>About The Body Explained</h1>
<p><strong>The Body Explained</strong> is an independent publication that turns trustworthy health and science information into clear, plain-English explainers. We focus on <em>evergreen</em> questions — how the body works, why we sleep, what nutrients actually do, how movement changes us — the kind of knowledge that stays useful for years.</p>
<h2>Our mission</h2>
<p>Good health information is often locked inside dense research papers or buried under hype. Our goal is simple: explain the science accurately, show our sources, and never sell miracle cures.</p>
<h2>How our content is made</h2>
<p>Articles are produced by the {SITE.editorial}. We use AI-assisted research and drafting tools, and every article is built from — and cross-checked against — reputable primary sources such as the U.S. National Institutes of Health (NIH), the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), the World Health Organization (WHO), peer-reviewed journals and major academic medical centers. Every article lists its sources so you can verify the information yourself.</p>
<p>Read our full <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> to learn what we cover, what we deliberately do not cover, and how we correct mistakes.</p>
<h2>What we are not</h2>
<p>We are not doctors and we do not provide medical advice, diagnosis or treatment. Our content is educational. Please read our <a href="/medical-disclaimer/">Medical Disclaimer</a>.</p>
<h2>Get in touch</h2>
<p>Spotted an error or have a question you'd like explained? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
